@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law ss 69, 69A and 71. Row IL-33. Source lines 836-851.
--
-- s 69  to whom the child allowance is paid (the mother, the father, a guardian ...);
-- s 69A the children of a man who has children by several women: in whose count each comes;
-- s 71  the insured parent died or ceased to be insured: by virtue of whom the allowance is paid.
--
-- Row IL-06 declines s 69A and s 71 by name ("named refusals consulted before s 67 answers") and does not
-- encode s 69. This module gives the three their own answers. It does not edit IL-06: how IL-06 then
-- counts, and at what amount, is for the capstone (NOTES.md, "What the capstone would need").
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 69 — to whom the allowance is paid`

-- src:837 | (א) קצבת ילדים תשולם לאם, אולם אם הילד נמצא עם האב בלבד, והאב זכאי לקצבה, תשולם הקצבה לאב.
-- src:838 | (ב) המוסד ישלם את הקצבה להורה, אף אם לא נתקיימו בו התנאים לפי סעיף קטן (א) אם ביקש זאת ההורה שמשתלמת לו הקצבה לפי הסעיף הקטן האמור.
-- src:839 | (ג) לא נתמלאו התנאים של סעיף קטן (א) לגבי שני ההורים, תשולם הקצבה בעד הילד לאפוטרופוס שנתמנה כדין, ובאין אפוטרופוס – למי שנתמנה לכך לפי סעיף 304(א).
-- src:840 | (ד) גם אם נתמלאו התנאים של סעיף קטן (א) רשאי המוסד, אם טובת הילד מחייבת זאת, לשלם את הקצבה להורה שני שאינו בר־הקצבה, או לאפוטרופוס או למי שנתמנה לכך לפי סעיף 304(א).
-- (a) to the mother; but if the child is with the father only and he is entitled, to the father. (b) the
-- Institute pays the other parent, even if (a) does not give him the allowance, if the parent paid under
-- (a) asks. (c) if (a) is met by neither parent, to the lawfully appointed guardian, and without one, to
-- the person appointed under s 304(a). (d) even if (a) is met, the Institute may, if the child's welfare
-- requires, pay a second parent who is not entitled, the guardian or the appointee.
--
-- FORKS. P1: "האם" / "האב" (the mother, the father) and a child with two parents of one sex, or with none
-- that the section can name: the text does not say; declined by name. A child with no parent at all is
-- (c): "the conditions of (a) are not met for both parents". P2: a request under (b) ("shall pay") and a
-- decision under (d) ("may") together: declined unless one is named to prevail (nouns).
-- NOT A FORK (class (b), only one reading arguable): that (a) pays the mother whether or not she is herself
-- entitled. The allowance is the insured parent's by ss 66-67; (a) is about whom it is paid to, and reading
-- (a) as paying only an entitled mother leaves the case of an entitled father and a mother who is not with
-- nobody to pay but a guardian.
@ref NII s 69(a), (c), lines 837, 839
GIVEN f IS A `The facts of section 69`
GIVETH A `The person to whom the child allowance is paid`
`s 69(a) and (c) — the payee before any request or decision, in` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the parents`
    WHEN `a mother and a father` THEN
        IF   f's `the child is with the father only` AND f's `the father is entitled to the allowance`
        THEN `the father`
        ELSE `the mother`
    WHEN `a mother only` THEN `the mother`
    WHEN `a father only` THEN
        IF   f's `the child is with the father only` AND f's `the father is entitled to the allowance`
        THEN `the father`
        ELSE underC
    WHEN `no parent` THEN underC
    WHEN `two parents of one sex` THEN
        REFUSE "section 69 pays the mother, or the father if the child is with him only; it does not say whom it pays where the child's two parents are of one sex"
    WHERE
        underC MEANS
            IF   f's `a guardian was lawfully appointed`
            THEN `the guardian lawfully appointed`
            ELSE IF   f's `a person was appointed under section 304(a)`
                 THEN `the person appointed under section 304(a)`
                 ELSE REFUSE "section 69(c) pays the lawfully appointed guardian and, without one, the person appointed under section 304(a); the case has neither"

@ref NII s 69(d), line 840
GIVEN d IS A `A decision of the Institute under section 69(d)`
GIVETH A `The person to whom the child allowance is paid`
`s 69(d) — the payee the Institute's decision names:` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `to pay a second parent who is not entitled` THEN `a second parent who is not entitled, by decision of the Institute`
    WHEN `to pay the guardian`                         THEN `the guardian lawfully appointed`
    WHEN `to pay the person appointed under section 304(a)` THEN `the person appointed under section 304(a)`

@ref NII s 69(a) to (d), lines 837-840; fork P2
GIVEN f  IS A `The facts of section 69`
      rd IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A `The person to whom the child allowance is paid`
`s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` f `, reading` rd MEANS
    CONSIDER (f's `the Institute's decision under section 69(d)`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN withoutDecision
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF   NOT f's `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`
        THEN `s 69(d) — the payee the Institute's decision names:` d
        ELSE CONSIDER rd's `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)`
             WHEN `the request under section 69(b) prevails` THEN requested
             WHEN `the decision under section 69(d) prevails` THEN `s 69(d) — the payee the Institute's decision names:` d
             WHEN `declined where the two differ` THEN
                 IF   requested EQUALS `s 69(d) — the payee the Institute's decision names:` d
                 THEN requested
                 ELSE REFUSE "section 69(b) says the Institute shall pay the other parent when the parent paid under (a) asks it; section 69(d) says it may pay another person if the child's welfare requires; the case has both a request and a decision, and the text does not say which prevails"
    WHERE
        base MEANS `s 69(a) and (c) — the payee before any request or decision, in` f
        requested MEANS `s 69(b) — the other parent, at the request of the parent paid under (a)`
        -- (b) applies where (a) paid a parent: the answer says it is paid to the other parent at the request.
        withoutDecision MEANS
            IF   f's `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`
            THEN CONSIDER base
                 WHEN `the mother` THEN requested
                 WHEN `the father` THEN requested
                 OTHERWISE REFUSE "section 69(b) speaks of the parent paid under (a) asking that the other parent be paid; the case has no parent paid under (a)"
            ELSE base

@ref NII s 69(b), line 838
GIVETH A `The person to whom the child allowance is paid`
`s 69(b) — the other parent, at the request of the parent paid under (a)` MEANS
    `the other parent, at the request of the parent paid under section 69(a)`

@ref NII s 69; the ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN f IS A `The facts of section 69`
GIVETH A `The person to whom the child allowance is paid`
`s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` f MEANS
    `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` f `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Section 69A — a man with children by several women`

-- src:843 | על אף האמור בכל מקום אחר בסימן זה, היו למבוטח ילדים ממספר נשים יחולו לגביו הוראות אלה:
-- src:844 | (1) היה לו ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב), יבואו הילדים במניין כל אחת מהנשים בנפרד;
-- src:845 | (2) לא היה לו ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב), יבואו הילדים במניין האב; הוכיחה האם, להנחת דעתו של המוסד, כי אינה מקיימת משק בית משותף עם האב, וכי הילד לא סמוך על שולחנו של האב – יבוא הילד במניין האם.
-- "על אף האמור בכל מקום אחר בסימן זה, היו למבוטח ילדים ממספר נשים יחולו לגביו הוראות אלה:
-- (1) היה לו ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב), יבואו הילדים במניין כל אחת מהנשים בנפרד;
-- (2) לא היה לו ילד כאמור בסעיף 68(ב), יבואו הילדים במניין האב; הוכיחה האם, להנחת דעתו של המוסד, כי אינה
--     מקיימת משק בית משותף עם האב, וכי הילד לא סמוך על שולחנו של האב – יבוא הילד במניין האם."
--
-- "A child as in section 68(b)": born before 1 June 2003 and the fourth or later in the count of the
-- parent's children. The count is ordered eldest first (as row IL-06's F4), so the children born before
-- 1 June 2003 hold the first places, and one of them is the fourth or later exactly when four or more were
-- born before that day. Whose count measures that, when s 69A is what decides the counts, is fork A1.
-- The list given is the man's children who are children within s 65 (row IL-06 decides that).
@ref NII s 68(b), s 69A(1), lines 821-822, 844
GIVEN c IS A `A child of a man with children by several women`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 68(b) — born before 1 June 2003:` c MEANS
    (c's `date of birth`) LESS THAN YMD 2003 6 1

@ref NII s 69A, line 843
GIVEN children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 69A — the names of the mothers of` children MEANS
    nub (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the name of the child's mother`) children)

@ref NII s 69A, line 843: "ילדים ממספר נשים"
GIVEN children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69A — the man has children by more than one woman:` children MEANS
    count (`s 69A — the names of the mothers of` children) GREATER THAN 1

@ref NII s 69A(1), line 844; fork A1
GIVEN children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69A(1) — four or more of all the man's children were born before 1 June 2003:` children MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `s 68(b) — born before 1 June 2003:` c) children) AT LEAST 4

@ref NII s 69A(1), line 844; fork A1
GIVEN children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69A(1) — some woman has four or more of her children born before 1 June 2003:` children MEANS
    any (GIVEN mother YIELD
            count (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the name of the child's mother` EQUALS mother AND `s 68(b) — born before 1 June 2003:` c) children) AT LEAST 4)
        (`s 69A — the names of the mothers of` children)

@ref NII s 69A(1), line 844; fork A1
GIVEN children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
      rd       IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` children `, reading` rd MEANS
    CONSIDER rd's `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)`
    WHEN `measured in the count of all the man's children` THEN allCount
    WHEN `measured in the count of each woman's children`  THEN eachCount
    WHEN `declined where the two readings differ` THEN
        IF   allCount EQUALS eachCount
        THEN allCount
        ELSE REFUSE "section 69A(1) asks whether the man has a child as in section 68(b), the fourth or later in the count of the parent's children born before 1 June 2003; section 69A is what decides the counts, so the text does not say whether that count is of all his children or of each woman's"
    WHERE
        allCount  MEANS `s 69A(1) — four or more of all the man's children were born before 1 June 2003:` children
        eachCount MEANS `s 69A(1) — some woman has four or more of her children born before 1 June 2003:` children

@ref NII s 69A(1), (2), lines 844-845
GIVEN c        IS A `A child of a man with children by several women`
      children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
      rd       IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A `The count in which a child comes under section 69A`
`s 69A — the count in which` c `comes, among` children `, reading` rd MEANS
    IF   `s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` children `, reading` rd
    THEN `the count of its mother`
    ELSE IF   c's `the mother proved to the Institute's satisfaction that she keeps no joint household with the father and that the child does not depend on his table`
         THEN `the count of its mother`
         ELSE `the count of the father`

@ref NII s 69A; the ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN c        IS A `A child of a man with children by several women`
      children IS A LIST OF `A child of a man with children by several women`
GIVETH A `The count in which a child comes under section 69A`
`s 69A — the count in which` c `comes, among` children MEANS
    `s 69A — the count in which` c `comes, among` children `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Section 71 — a parent who died or ceased to be insured`

-- src:851 | מת ההורה המבוטח או חדל להיות מבוטח, תשתלם מכוחו קצבת הילדים שהיתה משתלמת בעד הילד אילולא מת או אילולא חדל להיות מבוטח; ואולם אם היה לילד הורה שני, והוא זכאי לקצבה תשולם הקצבה מכוחו של ההורה השני.
-- "מת ההורה המבוטח או חדל להיות מבוטח, תשתלם מכוחו קצבת הילדים שהיתה משתלמת בעד הילד אילולא מת או אילולא
-- חדל להיות מבוטח; ואולם אם היה לילד הורה שני, והוא זכאי לקצבה תשולם הקצבה מכוחו של ההורה השני."
--
-- The allowance is paid by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured, at the amount it would
-- have been had he lived and stayed insured (the capstone asks IL-06 for it in his name); but if the child
-- has a second parent who is entitled to the allowance, it is paid by virtue of the second parent.
-- Where both parents died or ceased to be insured the text does not say by virtue of which (fork S1).
@ref NII s 71, line 851
GIVEN f IS A `The facts of section 71`
GIVETH A `By virtue of whom the child allowance is paid under section 71`
`s 71 — by virtue of whom, one parent having died or ceased to be insured, in` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the name of the child's second parent`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
    WHEN JUST second THEN
        IF   f's `the second parent is entitled to the child allowance`
        THEN `by virtue of the second parent`
        ELSE `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`

-- Both parents died or ceased to be insured. Reading (i): the parent s 67(b) would choose if both were alive
-- and insured: the father, unless the child is with the mother only. Reading (ii): the parent who died or
-- ceased to be insured first (the same day: declined).
@ref NII s 71, s 67(b), lines 851, 818; fork S1
GIVEN f  IS A `The facts of section 71`
      rd IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A `By virtue of whom the child allowance is paid under section 71`
`s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` f `, reading` rd MEANS
    IF   NOT f's `the second parent also died or ceased to be insured`
    THEN `s 71 — by virtue of whom, one parent having died or ceased to be insured, in` f
    ELSE CONSIDER rd's `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured`
         WHEN `by virtue of the parent s 67(b) would choose if both were alive and insured` THEN byS67b
         WHEN `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured first` THEN byFirst
         WHEN `section 71 is declined where the readings differ` THEN
             IF   byS67b EQUALS byFirst
             THEN byS67b
             ELSE REFUSE "section 71 speaks of one parent who died or ceased to be insured and, if there is a second parent, of the second's entitlement; both parents died or ceased to be insured, and the text does not say by virtue of which the allowance is paid"
    WHERE
        -- by virtue of the first-named parent, or of the second, as section 67(b) would choose: the father unless the child is with the mother only
        fatherIsFirst MEANS f's `that parent is the child's father`
        chooseFather  MEANS NOT f's `the child is with the mother only`
        byS67b MEANS
            IF   fatherIsFirst EQUALS chooseFather
            THEN `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
            ELSE `by virtue of the second parent`
        byFirst MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `the day the second parent died or ceased to be insured`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "the second parent is said to have died or ceased to be insured and the case gives no day"
            WHEN JUST d2 THEN
                IF   (f's `the day he or she died or ceased to be insured`) LESS THAN d2
                THEN `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
                ELSE IF   d2 LESS THAN (f's `the day he or she died or ceased to be insured`)
                     THEN `by virtue of the second parent`
                     ELSE REFUSE "both parents died or ceased to be insured on one day, and section 71 does not say by virtue of which"

@ref NII s 71; the ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN f IS A `The facts of section 71`
GIVETH A `By virtue of whom the child allowance is paid under section 71`
`s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` f MEANS
    `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` f `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
